<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21504" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illectus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inl-</span></b> ), a, um, adj.
		in-lectus, from 2. lego. * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Not collected</i>, <i>not gathered
				together</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stipula illecta sunt spicae in messe dejectae
					necdum lectae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig. 50, 16, 30, § 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Not read</i>, <i>unread</i> (very
			rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si non accipiet scriptum illectumque remittet,
					Lecturam spera,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. A.
					A. 1, 469</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">App. Flor. 18</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
